[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（英音）]
[ti:The Olympic Games]
[00:13.78]When was the last time this country hosted the Olympic Games?
[00:21.27]The Olympic Games will be held in our country in four years' time.
[00:27.26]As a great many people will be visiting the country, the government will be building new hotels, an immense stadium, and a new Olympic-standard swimming pool.
[00:40.65]They will also be building new roads and a special railway line.
[00:47.15]The Games will be held just outside the capital and the whole area will be called 'Olympic City'.
[00:57.89]Workers will have completed the new roads by the end of this year.
[01:04.61]By the end of next year, they will have finished work on the new stadium.
[01:12.14]The fantastic modern buildings have been designed by Kurt Gunter.
[01:19.46]Everybody will be watching anxiously as the new buildings go up.
[01:25.15]We are all very excited and are looking forward to the Olympic Games because they have never been held before in this country.
